  "cpu_contract": {
    "execution": "Each claim is local physical x86-32 behavior if that instruction is reached and completes without fault. No live CPU state, segment descriptor, cell, provider, or callee body was queried.",
    "stack_attributes": "Each implicit stack ESP equation requires SS to have a 32-bit stack-address attribute at that particular instruction. Program language x86:LE:32 does not prove current SS. After every opaque call, SS/DS and all segment state and attributes are unconstrained again. With a 16-bit SS stack-address attribute the stated implicit-stack ESP formulas are not asserted. Explicit ADD ESP,12 is 32-bit register arithmetic independent of the SS stack-address attribute.",
    "current_memory_and_aliases": "Memory expressions use the current segment and memory at the named instruction execution time. A PUSH memory operand is read before its stack store, using the pre-decrement ESP for [ESP+4]. Potential aliasing does not justify reusing an earlier cell or entry-stack value. No memory validity, disjointness, frame identity, argument identity, or preservation is assumed.",
    "opaque_return_rule": "All four callees are opaque and none is proved to return. At each conditional continuation, every register including EAX/ESI/EBP/ESP, flags, segments/descriptors and memory is newly unconstrained. Symbols Q1..Q4 name only ESP at that particular return; no relation to entry ESP or earlier Q is asserted.",
    "entry_09": "For current entry ESP=T, E8 at BFBA09 writes BFBA0E to current SS:[T-4], sets ESP=T-4, and transfers to numeric C05B68. This local CALL preserves other general registers and arithmetic flags; the callee has no established preservation.",
    "continuation_0E_12": "If control resumes at BFBA0E with ESP=Q1, read V1 as the current dword at SS:[Q1+4] using the pre-push ESP. PUSH stores V1 to current SS:[Q1-4] and leaves ESP=Q1-4. E8 at BFBA12 writes BFBA17 to SS:[Q1-8] and transfers to numeric C059A8 with ESP=Q1-8. V1 is not authenticated as the original caller argument.",
    "continuation_17_1D": "If control resumes at BFBA17 with ESP=Q2, read V2 as the current dword at DS:[00E15580] before the PUSH stack store. PUSH writes V2 to current SS:[Q2-4] and leaves ESP=Q2-4. E8 at BFBA1D writes BFBA22 to SS:[Q2-8] and transfers to numeric C04FDE with ESP=Q2-8. The absolute cell address is encoded; its current contents, type and provider identity are unqueried.",
    "continuation_22_27": "If control resumes at BFBA22 with ESP=Q3 and EAX=A3, PUSH imm32 writes the 32-bit value 255 to SS:[Q3-4] and leaves ESP=Q3-4. The encoding is 68 FF000000, not a sign-extended imm8 -1. CALL EAX at BFBA27 uses the current A3 as its unresolved runtime target, writes BFBA29 to SS:[Q3-8], and transfers with ESP=Q3-8. It is register-indirect, not an extra memory dereference. These local instructions preserve other general registers including EBP and arithmetic flags.",
    "continuation_29_2C": "If control resumes at BFBA29 with ESP=Q4, ADD ESP,sign_extend(0x0C) sets R=(Q4+12) mod 2^32 and ESP=R; it performs no memory access and requires no SS stack-size assumption. It preserves other general registers and sets the arithmetic flags below. RET at BFBA2C then reads its unknown next EIP from current SS:[R] and, only with current SS stack-address size 32, leaves ESP=R+4 mod 2^32. RET preserves the ADD arithmetic flags. Neither the return target nor a restored original caller stack is authenticated.",
    "ADD_flags": {
